  <h1>Training Journal: Mostly Downs, and a Decision Rule</h1>
  <div class="postmeta">November 24, 2026 · Journal</div>

  <article>
    <p>Honest update: it has mostly been downs.</p>

    <p>My back has been really tight for a while. A planned half marathon
    training run got skipped because it was raining, and I decided I was not
    going out in it. I have not run a single 5K in this build. Then there was
    the half marathon on November 21. I had run a good one a few weeks earlier,
    1:49:56, and this one came in at 1:57:33. A dumbbell had glanced off my
    quad at the gym days before. I figured it was nothing, and about 5 miles
    into the race it let me know otherwise. It turned out to be a bruise and
    nothing more, and there has been no pain since. The real damage was that I
    could not tell where my fitness actually is.</p>

    <p>The back is the bigger worry. The community pool heater has been broken
    for more than a month, and a warm pool is what normally helps it.</p>

    <h2>Where my head is</h2>
    <p>There is a marathon on December 12, and I am thinking of it as a
    training run for a marathon in January. I can always finish a marathon.
    What I do not know is how long it takes, and how my back holds up over
    26.2.</p>

    <p>So I am not forcing it. Two things decide it: whether I can get a Black
    Friday discount on the entry, and how the Thanksgiving Day run feels. If I
    get to the end of it feeling like I can make this happen, I am in.</p>

    <p>If you want to see what that day looks like on paper, the
    <a href="/?d=marathon&amp;u=mi&amp;mode=even&amp;t=4:05:00&amp;eq=half&amp;eqt=1:49:56&amp;profile=1.090">finish plan is here</a>,
    about 9:20 per mile. I will report back after Thanksgiving.</p>
